# nr-office-design-discipline: what the wiring applies for the new crate mixdog-office-design.
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change: the crate is pure and has no caller yet.)

# 1. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace] members: add after the line `    "crates/mixdog-office-base",`
    "crates/mixdog-office-design",

# 2. native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies]: add after the line
#    `mixdog-office-base = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-base" }`
mixdog-office-design = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-design" }

# 3. native/core/Cargo.lock: `cargo update --workspace --offline` adds the package `mixdog-office-design` with the
#    dependencies mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-workspace-hack, serde_json (all already in the lock; no new
#    external crate and no new feature of one).

# 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml: `cargo hakari generate` (the new crate depends on the hack
#    package through its own Cargo.toml; it adds no third-party dependency of its own).

# 5. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; after "office-detect"):
    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-discipline.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-discipline/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "eabd40749c80fbb1aa0d1cbae3b1dd555642689a4bc19a8db75dd10dc00e3991",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-discipline.mjs",
      "set": "office-discipline",
      "totalBytes": 1796840
    },

# 6. For the later tasks of the track (nr-office-design-composition, -docx, -xlsx, -library): the crate exports
#    `tokens::resolve_office_design(format, &request, library: Option<&Value>, &CompositionContext)`. The composition
#    context (purpose, expression_mode, recent_compositions) is the answer of `resolveOfficeCompositionContext`, which
#    is composition-system.mjs (task nr-office-design-composition): that task adds `resolve_office_composition_context`
#    and its callers pass the result in. Nothing here depends on that module.
